fix(interp): Prevent double-wrapping of `_Return` values in `HirStmt::Return`

- **crates/vox-compiler/src/eval/stmt.rs**: Modified `eval_stmt` to check if the value being returned by `HirStmt::Return` is already a `_Return` sentinel. If it is, the value is propagated as-is to prevent double-wrapping (e.g., `_Return(_Return(..))`), which caused `_Return` values to leak to callers when an inner `return` or `?` produced an early-return sentinel within a returned expression. This fixes a bug surfaced by `classify(404)` in `match_arm_stmts.vox`.

